{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Client-Side Paging.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Client-Side Paging.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"client side paging client side paging","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Client-Side Paging.md","fileName":"Client-Side Paging.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Client-Side Paging","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 20:34\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Web Data Query and Presentation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Web Data Query and Presentation","Server-Side Paging","aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Client-Side Paging.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Client-Side Paging.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"client side paging client side paging","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Client-Side Paging.md","fileName":"Client-Side Paging.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Client-Side Paging","heading":"Client-Side Paging","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Client-side paging fetches a complete result set and divides it into pages inside the browser. Page changes are fast after the initial response because they do not require another server request.\n\nThe approach becomes inefficient when the dataset is large: the server still queries and transfers every row, and the client stores and processes values the user may never view. [[Server-Side Paging]] avoids that cost by requesting one slice at a time.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Web Data Query and Presentation","Server-Side Paging","aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Client-Side Paging.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Client-Side Paging.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"client side paging client side paging","fi